  "__comment": "Body follows Create's mechanical crafter: two slabs with a gap at z 6-10 and four thin rims. crafter_side has a transparent window at rows 6-9 which Create never samples - the gap in the geometry is where the mechanism shows, and ours shows the cogwheel. Every crafter_side face carries Create's own face rotation; without it a 16x6 uv region lands transposed on a 6x16 face and the sides stretch. The back is the gearbox face at two depths only: the 2px perimeter and the shaft's 4x4 sit at the block face, everything between them is one pixel in. The shaft and the cogwheel are not here: they turn, so they live in block/p_grid_kinetics and are drawn by the block entity's Flywheel visual.",
